    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0096",
      "sequence": 108,
      "meaning": "The reception party escorts the procession to lovely guest quarters. Mainā prepares an auspicious ārati and goes joyfully to welcome Hara with women singing benedictions and a golden tray holding excellent water. At the sight of Rudra’s fearsome guise, terror fills the women and they flee indoors; Maheśa returns to the lodging. Heavy grief fills Mainā. She summons the mountain’s daughter, seats her tenderly in her lap and weeps from lotus-dark eyes: how could the dull creator who gave her such beauty choose a mad groom? It is like forcing the fruit meant for a wish-tree onto a thorny babūl. She vows sooner to leap from the mountain with her daughter, burn in fire, drown in the ocean or let home and reputation perish than arrange this marriage while alive. Seeing the mountain queen lament and weep from love for her daughter, all the women become distraught.",
