    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0098",
      "sequence": 110,
      "meaning": "Nārada then consoles everyone by recounting the earlier story. He tells Mainā truly that her daughter Bhavānī is Jagadambā: unborn, beginningless, imperishable Power, forever dwelling as half of Śambhu. She causes the world’s creation, preservation and dissolution and assumes playful bodies by her own will. First she was born in Dakṣa’s house as beautiful Satī and married Śaṅkara, as the whole world knows. Once, traveling with Śiva, she saw Rāma, sun of the Raghu lotus. Deluded, she rejected Śiva’s counsel and, under confusion, assumed Sītā’s guise.",
