      "sequence": 111,
      "meaning": "Mainā and Himālaya rejoice and repeatedly bow at Pārvatī’s feet. Every woman, man, child, youth and elder in the city is delighted. Auspicious songs arise, varied golden vessels are arranged, and many kinds of feast are prepared according to culinary teaching and custom. Who could describe a banquet in the home where Mother Bhavānī dwells? All wedding guests—Viṣṇu, Brahmā and gods of every class—are respectfully summoned and seated in varied rows. Skilled cooks begin serving, while groups of women, knowing the gods are eating, offer gentle, playful wedding taunts.",
