      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0100",
      "sequence": 112,
      "meaning": "All the gods are respectfully received and given fitting seats. The altar is decorated according to Vedic rule as women sing beautiful benedictions. Brahmā creates an indescribably divine throne. Śiva sits after bowing to the Brahmins, remembering his Lord Raghurāya within. Great sages summon Umā, and her companions bring her adorned. Her beauty entrances every god; what poet in the world could describe it? Recognizing Bhavānī as Jagadambikā and Śiva’s beloved, the gods bow inwardly. Even millions of mouths could not describe the very limit of beauty embodied in her.",
